{
 "dur": 71.6,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "How does a steel box",
    "carry you up a hundred floors?",
    "Let's take",
    "an elevator apart."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 5.85,
   "chunks": [
    "This is a traction elevator.",
    "The car rides up and down the shaft,",
    "hung from steel hoist ropes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 12.08,
   "chunks": [
    "Up top, the ropes wrap",
    "over a grooved wheel called the sheave.",
    "An electric motor turns it,",
    "and friction in the grooves does the lifting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 20.35,
   "chunks": [
    "On the other end of the ropes",
    "hangs the counterweight.",
    "It weighs about as much as the car,",
    "plus 40% of a full load."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 28.03,
   "chunks": [
    "So the motor never",
    "lifts the whole car.",
    "It only moves the difference."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 32.65,
   "chunks": [
    "Guide rails run",
    "the full height of the shaft,",
    "keeping the car and counterweight",
    "on track."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 38.1,
   "chunks": [
    "Codes require",
    "at least three hoist ropes,",
    "each built with",
    "a huge safety margin."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 43.61,
   "chunks": [
    "But what if",
    "the car starts falling?",
    "Up top, a governor watches the speed.",
    "Too fast, and it trips."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 50.03,
   "chunks": [
    "It grabs its own rope,",
    "which yanks the safety brakes.",
    "Steel wedges bite the guide rails",
    "and stop the car."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 57.49,
   "chunks": [
    "In 1854, in New York,",
    "Elisha Otis stood on a raised platform",
    "and had its rope cut.",
    "It dropped a few inches, then held."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 66.89,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "the elevator."
   ]
  }
 ]
}